## Parent

Part of #90

## What to build

Build the source viewer as a side panel beside chat and bottom sheet on small screens. Render server-provided text and tables with highlight information, scroll to the highlight with surrounding context, show document title, category, period, version, status, and page indicator, multi-citation Next/Previous navigation with J/K shortcuts, newer-version banner, unavailable or lost-access message, copy citation and report-wrong-source footer controls, and Open full document action when available. The viewer must be keyboard accessible with visible focus ring and close on Esc.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Cited text is highlighted, or cited tables render as real tables with relevant cell or row highlighting
- [ ] Viewer scrolls to the highlight and supports surrounding context
- [ ] Next/Previous and J/K move through multiple citations on one chip
- [ ] Newer-version banner appears when the cited version is not the latest
- [ ] Unavailable or lost-access sources show the non-leaking not-available message
- [ ] Copy citation and report wrong source controls work from the footer
- [ ] Open full document calls only the original-file endpoint when permitted
- [ ] Keyboard navigation, visible focus, Esc close, and mobile bottom sheet work
- [ ] All states (loading, empty, error, success) are handled and tested
